{"id": "C47", "type": "cross_filing", "question": "In Microsoft's fiscal 2025 cash flow statement, did the depreciation, amortization, and other add-back change between the fiscal 2025 and fiscal 2026 annual reports?", "answer": "Yes. It was $34,153 million as first filed and $29,433 million in the fiscal 2026 10-K, a cut of $4,720 million, offset by a matching rise in net recognized losses on investments and derivatives (609 to 5,329); cash from operations is unchanged at $136,162 million.", "answer_value": -4720000000, "answer_unit": "USD", "tolerance": 0, "supporting_facts": [{"doc": "MSFT_FY2025_10K", "page": 53, "label": "Depreciation, amortization, and other", "period": "fiscal year ended June 30, 2025 (as filed in FY2025 10-K)", "printed": "34,153", "scale": "millions", "value": 34153000000}, {"doc": "MSFT_FY2026_10K", "page": 53, "label": "Depreciation, amortization, and other", "period": "fiscal year ended June 30, 2025 (comparative in FY2026 10-K)", "printed": "29,433", "scale": "millions", "value": 29433000000}, {"doc": "MSFT_FY2025_10K", "page": 53, "label": "Net recognized losses on investments and derivatives", "period": "fiscal 2025 as filed", "printed": "609", "scale": "millions", "value": 609000000}, {"doc": "MSFT_FY2026_10K", "page": 53, "label": "Net recognized losses (gains) on investments and derivatives", "period": "fiscal 2025 comparative", "printed": "5,329", "scale": "millions", "value": 5329000000}, {"doc": "MSFT_FY2026_10K", "page": 53, "label": "Net cash from operations", "period": "fiscal 2025 comparative", "printed": "136,162", "scale": "millions", "value": 136162000000}], "derivation": "29,433 - 34,153 = -4,720; 5,329 - 609 = +4,720; net cash from operations 136,162 in both.", "tags": ["restated", "fiscal_year_trap"], "notes": "Reclassification within operating activities; Note 1 of the FY2026 10-K (PDF page 55) says prior period cash flow amounts were recast. Microsoft fiscal 2025 ended June 30, 2025."}
